{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number, which represents the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    It uses Stirling numbers of the second kind to compute the result.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] will store the Stirling number of the second kind S(i, j)\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: S(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Calculate Stirling numbers S(i, j) using the recurrence relation:\n    # S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + j * dp[i-1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n\n    bell_n = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += dp[n][k]\n\n    return bell_n"}
