{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "_memo = {}\n\ndef sequence(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        # Apply the recursive formula P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1))\n        p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n        p_p_n_minus_1 = sequence(p_n_minus_1)\n        p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n        result = p_p_n_minus_1 + p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/87", "solution": "def merge_dictionaries_three(\n    dict1: dict,\n    dict2: dict,\n    dict3: dict\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges three dictionaries into a single dictionary.\n\n    The merge logic prioritizes dictionaries in the order they are provided:\n    1. All key-value pairs from dict1 are included.\n    2. Key-value pairs from dict2 are added only if their keys do not already exist in the merged dictionary.\n    3. Key-value pairs from dict3 are added only if their keys do not already exist in the merged dictionary.\n    \"\"\"\n    merged_dict = dict(dict1)\n\n    for key, value in dict2.items():\n        if key not in merged_dict:\n            merged_dict[key] = value\n\n    for key, value in dict3.items():\n        if key not in merged_dict:\n            merged_dict[key] = value\n\n    return merged_dict"}
