{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer is an undulating number.\n    An undulating number is one where digits alternate, e.g., A B A B A.\"\"\"\n\n    def _convert_to_digits(num: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Converts a positive integer into a list of its digits.\"\"\"\n        return [int(d) for d in str(num)]\n\n    digits = _convert_to_digits(number)\n    n = len(digits)\n\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    # An undulating number has the pattern A B A B...\n    # This means digit[i] == digit[i+2] and digit[i] != digit[i+1]\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        if not (digits[i] == digits[i+2] and digits[i] != digits[i+1]):\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "def divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of positive divisors for a given integer n.\n    It iterates up to the square root of n to find divisor pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    i = 1\n    while i * i <= n:\n        if n % i == 0:\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1\n            else:\n                count += 2\n        i += 1\n    return count"}
