{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "def next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    Handles the special case where n is 0 by returning 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    power = 1\n    while power < n:\n        power *= 2\n    return power"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "class IndexOutOfBoundsError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an index is outside the valid bounds of a list.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Index out of bounds\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass InvalidRangeError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the start index is greater than the end index.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Start index cannot be greater than end index\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef sum_range_list(numbers: list, startIndex: int, endIndex: int) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified, inclusive range.\n    Raises IndexOutOfBoundsError or InvalidRangeError for invalid indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    if not (0 <= startIndex < n):\n        raise IndexOutOfBoundsError(\"Start index out of bounds\")\n    if not (0 <= endIndex < n):\n        raise IndexOutOfBoundsError(\"End index out of bounds\")\n    \n    if startIndex > endIndex:\n        raise InvalidRangeError(\"Start index cannot be greater than end index\")\n    \n    current_sum = 0\n    for i in range(startIndex, endIndex + 1):\n        current_sum += numbers[i]\n        \n    return current_sum"}
