{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list, n: int, x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the index if found, otherwise returns -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(arr: list, n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(arr, n, x)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False # Element not found in the array\n\n    # To be a majority element, it must appear at least (n // 2) + 1 times.\n    # If the first occurrence is at `first_idx`, then the element at `first_idx + n // 2`\n    # must also be `x` for `x` to be a majority element.\n    majority_check_idx = first_idx + n // 2\n\n    return majority_check_idx < n and arr[majority_check_idx] == x"}
