{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Helper for Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum contiguous subarray sum in a single array.\n    def kadane(current_arr):\n        max_current = current_arr[0]\n        max_global = current_arr[0]\n        for i in range(1, len(current_arr)):\n            max_current = max(current_arr[i], max_current + current_arr[i])\n            max_global = max(max_global, max_current)\n        return max_global\n\n    # Case 1: The array is repeated only once.\n    if k == 1:\n        return kadane(arr)\n\n    # Case 2: The array is repeated multiple times (k > 1).\n\n    # Calculate the maximum subarray sum within a single instance of arr.\n    max_single_array_sum = kadane(arr)\n\n    # Calculate the total sum of all elements in arr.\n    total_arr_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of any prefix subarray of arr.\n    current_sum_prefix = 0\n    max_prefix_sum = float('-inf')\n    for x in arr:\n        current_sum_prefix += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_sum_prefix)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum sum of any suffix subarray of arr.\n    current_sum_suffix = 0\n    max_suffix_sum = float('-inf')\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_sum_suffix += arr[i]\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_sum_suffix)\n\n    # Initialize the maximum possible sum found so far.\n    ans = max_single_array_sum\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive, repeating it multiple times\n    # can extend a subarray that spans across full repetitions.\n    if total_arr_sum > 0:\n        # The sum could be formed by a max suffix of the first array,\n        # (k-2) full repetitions of the array, and a max prefix of the last array.\n        ans = max(ans, max_prefix_sum + (k - 2) * total_arr_sum + max_suffix_sum)\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is non-positive, adding more full repetitions won't help.\n        # The maximum sum could span at most two array blocks (max suffix of first + max prefix of second).\n        ans = max(ans, max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum)\n\n    return ans"}
