{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def _calculate_digit_sum(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of digits for a single non-negative integer.\n    e.g., _calculate_digit_sum(56) == 11\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_sum = 0\n    # Handle the case of number 0 explicitly as the loop condition `number > 0` would skip it.\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n    while number > 0:\n        digit_sum += number % 10\n        number //= 10\n    return digit_sum\n\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits for each number in a given list\n    and returns the sum of these individual digit sums.\n    e.g., sum_of_digits([10, 2, 56]) == 14\n    \"\"\"\n    total_aggregated_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        total_aggregated_sum += _calculate_digit_sum(number)\n    return total_aggregated_sum"}
