{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(arr: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds a pair of integers with the highest product from a given array.\n\n    Args:\n        arr: A list of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple (int, int) representing the pair with the highest product.\n        Returns (None, None) if the array has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return (None, None)\n\n    max1 = -float('inf')\n    max2 = -float('inf')\n    min1 = float('inf')\n    min2 = float('inf')\n\n    for x in arr:\n        if x > max1:\n            max2 = max1\n            max1 = x\n        elif x > max2:\n            max2 = x\n\n        if x < min1:\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = x\n        elif x < min2:\n            min2 = x\n\n    product_of_two_largest = max1 * max2\n    product_of_two_smallest = min1 * min2\n\n    if product_of_two_largest >= product_of_two_smallest:\n        return (min(max1, max2), max(max1, max2))\n    else:\n        return (min(min1, min2), max(min1, min2))"}
