{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef sumofFactors(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all even factors for a given positive integer.\n    It iterates up to the square root of the number for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int) or num <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of num\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(num)) + 1):\n        if num % i == 0:\n            # i is a factor\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += i\n\n            # Calculate the corresponding factor pair\n            factor_pair = num // i\n            # Avoid double-counting if i * i == num (perfect square)\n            if i * i != num:\n                if factor_pair % 2 == 0:\n                    total_sum += factor_pair\n    return total_sum\n```"}
