{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all unique combinations of elements from an input list, including an empty list,\n    and returns them in a specific, predefined order using a recursive approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return [[]]\n\n    # Pop the last element for processing\n    last_element = input_list[-1]\n    remaining_list = input_list[:-1]\n\n    # Recursively get combinations for the rest of the list\n    combinations_without_last = combinations_list(remaining_list)\n\n    # Generate new combinations by adding the last element to existing ones\n    combinations_with_last = []\n    for combo in combinations_without_last:\n        combinations_with_last.append(combo + [last_element])\n\n    # Combine and order the results: combinations without the last element\n    # followed by combinations including the last element, maintaining the order.\n    # The order requirement is implicitly handled by the recursive structure and list concatenation.\n    return combinations_without_last + combinations_with_last"}
