{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def _normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Sorts elements within a tuple to create a normalized form.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(t))\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the intersection of two tuple lists, ignoring tuple element order.\n\n    Args:\n        list1: The first list of tuples.\n        list2: The second list of tuples.\n\n    Returns:\n        A set of unique tuples common to both lists, with elements sorted within each tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_set1 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    normalized_set2 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n    intersection_normalized = normalized_set1.intersection(normalized_set2)\n    return set(intersection_normalized)"}
