{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "from typing import Union\n\ndef first_Digit(number: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns the first digit of a given number.\n    Handles negative numbers and floats by finding the first non-zero digit.\n    \"\"\"\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    num_str = str(abs_number)\n\n    if '.' in num_str:\n        num_str = num_str.replace('.', '')\n\n    for char in num_str:\n        if char.isdigit() and char != '0':\n            return int(char)\n\n    return 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs (arr[i], arr[j]) with i < j whose bitwise XOR value is odd.\n    An XOR value is odd if one number is even and the other is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_xor_count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Calculate the bitwise XOR value of the pair\n            xor_value = arr[i] ^ arr[j]\n            # Check if the XOR value is odd\n            if xor_value % 2 != 0:\n                odd_xor_count += 1\n    return odd_xor_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first n natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the sum of the first n natural numbers using the formula n * (n + 1) / 2.\n    sum_of_naturals = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n    # Calculate the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers.\n    # This is equivalent to the square of the sum of natural numbers.\n    sum_of_cubes = sum_of_naturals ** 2\n\n    # Compute the difference and return the result.\n    result = sum_of_cubes - sum_of_naturals\n    return result"}
