{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the area of the largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle.\n\n    Returns None for negative radius.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    \n    # The largest triangle has its base equal to the diameter (2*radius)\n    # and its height equal to the radius. Area = (1/2) * base * height.\n    area = radius * radius\n    return area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    The median is the average of the two middle elements when combined.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2\n    m1 = -1  # To store the (size-1)-th element (0-indexed) of the combined list\n    m2 = -1  # To store the size-th element (0-indexed) of the combined list\n\n    # Iterate (size + 1) times to find the two middle elements of the combined list\n    # The combined list has 2*size elements. For an even number of elements,\n    # the median is the average of the elements at index (size-1) and size.\n    for count in range(size + 1):\n        m1 = m2  # m1 stores the element found in the previous iteration\n\n        if i == size:  # All elements of list1 have been processed\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size:  # All elements of list2 have been processed\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] < list2[j]:\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (float(m1) + float(m2)) / 2.0"}
