{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "def find_first_occurrence(array: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the lowest index at which the target appears, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential first occurrence\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an even earlier occurrence in the left half\n        elif array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1  # Target is in the right half\n        else:  # array[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1  # Target is in the left half\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of products of all possible contiguous sublists\n    for a given list of numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Extract the sublist from index i to j (inclusive)\n            sublist = numbers[i : j + 1]\n            # Calculate the product of elements in the sublist\n            product = math.prod(sublist)\n            # Add the product to the total sum\n            total_sum += product\n            \n    return total_sum"}
