{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "def toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles all bits of the number except the most significant bit and the least significant bit.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1: # Numbers with 0, 1, or 2 bits have no \"middle\" bits\n        return number\n\n    num_bits = number.bit_length()\n    if num_bits <= 2:\n        return number\n\n    # Create a mask with all bits set, then clear the MSB and LSB\n    # Example: num_bits = 4, middle_mask = 0110 (binary)\n    # 1 << num_bits creates a number with (num_bits + 1) bits, e.g., 10000 for num_bits=4\n    # (1 << num_bits) - 1 creates a mask with all num_bits set, e.g., 01111 for num_bits=4\n    # (1 << (num_bits - 1)) clears the MSB: ~(1 << (num_bits - 1))\n    # 1 clears the LSB: ~1\n    # Combining: (((1 << num_bits) - 1) ^ (1 << (num_bits - 1))) ^ 1\n    \n    # A simpler way:\n    # 1. Create a mask of all '1's up to num_bits: (1 << num_bits) - 1\n    # 2. Exclude the MSB by XORing with a mask that only has MSB set: ^ (1 << (num_bits - 1))\n    # 3. Exclude the LSB by XORing with a mask that only has LSB set: ^ 1\n    # This gives us a mask where only middle bits are set.\n    \n    # Example for number=9 (1001), num_bits=4\n    # all_set_mask = (1 << 4) - 1 = 15 (01111)\n    # msb_mask = (1 << (4 - 1)) = (1 << 3) = 8 (01000)\n    # lsb_mask = 1 (00001)\n    #\n    # mask_for_toggling = all_set_mask ^ msb_mask ^ lsb_mask\n    #                  = 01111 ^ 01000 ^ 00001\n    #                  = 00111 ^ 00001\n    #                  = 00110 (binary) = 6\n    #\n    # result = number ^ mask_for_toggling\n    #        = 01001 ^ 00110\n    #        = 01111 = 15\n\n    msb_mask = 1 << (num_bits - 1)\n    lsb_mask = 1\n    \n    # Create a mask with all bits set from 0 to num_bits-1\n    all_bits_mask = (1 << num_bits) - 1\n    \n    # Remove MSB and LSB from the all_bits_mask to get the middle_bits_mask\n    # This mask will have 1s only where middle bits are located.\n    middle_bits_mask = all_bits_mask ^ msb_mask ^ lsb_mask\n\n    return number ^ middle_bits_mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(sorted_list: list[int], value: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
