{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "class _NumberChecker:\n    def __init__(self, number: int):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the _NumberChecker with the given number and extracts its digits.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._value = number\n        self._digits = self._extract_digits(number)\n\n    def contains_zero(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if the number contains the digit zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        return 0 in self._digits\n\n    def is_divisible_by_all_digits(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Verifies if the number is perfectly divisible by every one of its constituent digits.\n        \"\"\"\n        for digit in self._digits:\n            if self._value % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _extract_digits(self, number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper method to extract constituent digits of a number.\n        \"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_num = abs(number)\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range [startnum, endnum] where every number\n    is divisible by every non-zero digit it contains. Numbers containing\n    the digit zero are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for n in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        checker = _NumberChecker(n)\n        if not checker.contains_zero() and checker.is_divisible_by_all_digits():\n            results.append(n)\n    return results"}
