{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "from typing import List, TypeVar, Union\n\nComparable = TypeVar('Comparable', bound=Union[int, float, str])\n\ndef right_insertion(sorted_list: List[Comparable], value: Comparable) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    It returns the index where `value` can be inserted to maintain sorted order, specifically after any existing equal elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
