{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr: list, target: any) -> int:\n    # Finds the last position of a given element in a sorted array using a binary search variant.\n    # Returns the index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find a further occurrence in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate from max(1, l) to r (inclusive) to consider only natural numbers.\n    for num in range(max(1, l), r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum"}
