{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer.\"\"\"\n    BIT_LENGTH = 32\n    d = d % BIT_LENGTH\n    # Perform the left shift\n    left_shifted = (number << d)\n    # Get the bits that wrapped around from the left shift\n    wrapped_around = (number >> (BIT_LENGTH - d))\n    # Combine the left-shifted part with the wrapped-around part\n    result = (left_shifted | wrapped_around)\n    # Ensure the result is within 32 bits\n    return result & ((1 << BIT_LENGTH) - 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "solution": "def test_three_equal(num1, num2, num3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of equal integers among three given inputs.\n    Returns 3 if all three are equal, 2 if exactly two are equal, and 0 if all are distinct.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num1 == num2 == num3:\n        return 3\n    elif num1 == num2 or num1 == num3 or num2 == num3:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 0"}
